---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectShots from '../../components/ProjectShots.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Symferium — Michal Malček"
  description="Symferium: a local multi-model AI runtime for Apple Silicon."
  back={{ href: `${base}portfolio/`, label: 'Portfolio' }}
>
  <header class="pt-10 pb-8 border-b border-line">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(35px,4.8vw,52px)] font-semibold tracking-tight m-0 mb-3">Symferium</h1>
    <p class="lede m-0">A standalone local AI runtime for Apple Silicon: it downloads, loads and unloads many models at once, serves each one on its own localhost port with an OpenAI-compatible API, and keeps every load inside a memory budget measured on the machine.</p>
  </header>

  <Section id="intro" title="Intro" note="features">
    <ul class="m-0 pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2 text-[17.5px] text-fg-dim leading-snug list-disc">
      <li>Symferium is a local multi-model AI runtime for Apple Silicon: one Rust daemon picks the engine, watches the memory budget, and serves a browser UI plus an agent API.</li>
      <li>The catalog covers llama.cpp, MLX, mlx-vlm, whisper.cpp, ONNX and llamacpp-turboquant, with models pulled through the Hugging Face API.</li>
      <li>TurboQuant (turbo3) produced coherent text at about 10.5 tokens/s on this hardware.</li>
      <li>A governor selects the model, checks the cache and switches engines from the machine's performance profile.</li>
      <li>It is managed from a browser UI and from a local API that agents can use.</li>
      <li>The daemon serves :7700 (UI + control API: /api/machine, /api/models, /api/load, /api/unload, /api/settings, /api/catalog/*, /api/downloads, /api/bench, /api/presets, /api/events (SSE), /api/tools) and :7701… one port per loaded model (OpenAI routes of the engine behind it, plus /health and /v1/models).</li>
      <li>Engines are profiles in the config (binary + argument templates), so any flag is visible and editable: llamacpp (llama-server, GGUF chat, vision, embeddings, rerank), llamacpp-turboquant (TurboQuant fork, off), mlx / mlx-vlm / rapid-mlx (off), whispercpp, parakeet (long-form, 25 languages incl. EN + SK in one checkpoint), tts (Kokoro, Piper).</li>
      <li>The Parakeet sidecar loads the checkpoint once and keeps it resident, so a 50-minute podcast is one request. It uses the encoder's local-attention mode by default.</li>
      <li>Install on the Mac: scripts/install.sh (Homebrew llama.cpp + whisper-cpp, uv Python env for MLX/TTS, binary, LaunchAgent). open http://127.0.0.1:7700/</li>
      <li>Factorium's running inference (:8080, :8083, :8084) is not touched. Its model folder (~/.factorium/models) is scanned read-only, so nothing is downloaded twice.</li>
      <li>A load that does not fit is refused with HTTP 409 and every number (weights, KV cache, checkpoints, compute, overhead, headroom). Agents read GET /api/tools and call POST /api/tools/{"{"}name{"}"}; they may change only settings marked agent_writable.</li>
      <li>CLI: symferium serve [--no-restore], probe, models, estimate, bench, launchd install|uninstall|print, config [--show].</li>
      <li>Develop: cargo test (unit + end-to-end against a mock engine), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <ProjectShots slug="symferium" alt="Symferium" part="hero" />

  <Section id="links" title="Download and links" note="links">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-[17px]">
      <a href="https://github.com/misomalcek/symferium/">Repository</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/misomalcek/symferium/blob/main/README.md">README</a>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="results" title="Results" note="measured">
    <ul class="m-0 pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2 text-[17.5px] text-fg-dim leading-snug list-disc">
      <li>Multi-Model Inference Runtime: developed a dedicated AI runtime for Apple Silicon that manages model lifecycles, memory budgets and engine selection (Llama.cpp, MLX, Whisper) via a unified Rust daemon.</li>
      <li>TurboQuant Optimization: successfully implemented and verified TurboQuant (turbo3) inference, achieving coherent text generation at about 10.5 tok/s on local hardware.</li>
      <li>Model Governance: engineered a "Governor" system to handle model selection, cache validation and automated engine switching based on hardware-specific performance profiles.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <ProjectShots slug="symferium" alt="Symferium" part="gallery" />
</Base>
